{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43788600",
      "title": "Outputting Conditional Content",
      "lectureOrder": 43,
      "videoOrder": 39,
      "sourceHash": "9dd3616367ade26ff89b0919507f333ac947da5387f5dce4db7e08470c01ce69",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.3,
          "end": 2.28,
          "en": "So outputting list data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.28,
          "end": 5.16,
          "en": "is an important Angular feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.16,
          "end": 7.89,
          "en": "But another important Angular feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.89,
          "end": 11.34,
          "en": "which you'll also use in templates a lot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.34,
          "end": 15.33,
          "en": "is being able to output conditional content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.33,
          "end": 18.06,
          "en": "so content that should only be rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.06,
          "end": 20.283,
          "en": "under certain circumstances.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.27,
          "end": 24.75,
          "en": "For example, here, this tasks component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.75,
          "end": 29.22,
          "en": "because we might not always have a selectedUser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.22,
          "end": 32.4,
          "en": "Now at the moment in our app, we indeed do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.4,
          "end": 34.2,
          "en": "but we can easily change this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.2,
          "end": 37.86,
          "en": "by going to the app component TypeScript file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.86,
          "end": 41.46,
          "en": "and there, instead of setting the selectedUserId",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.46,
          "end": 46.44,
          "en": "to an initial value of u1, we could set it up like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.44,
          "end": 49.143,
          "en": "and not give it an initial value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.07,
          "end": 52.8,
          "en": "In that case, we have to define the type of value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.8,
          "end": 56.49,
          "en": "it will eventually hold, which would be a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.49,
          "end": 60.12,
          "en": "and we have to add a question mark here to tell TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.12,
          "end": 63.243,
          "en": "that it's fine that this might not be set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.29,
          "end": 66.39,
          "en": "But with that change made,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.39,
          "end": 69.543,
          "en": "we now indeed not always have a selected user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.19,
          "end": 72.72,
          "en": "and we then might not want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.72,
          "end": 75.57,
          "en": "to render this tasks component at all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.57,
          "end": 77.58,
          "en": "because at the moment, we would render it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.58,
          "end": 80.94,
          "en": "and essentially show nothing for the user's name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.94,
          "end": 83.97,
          "en": "But if you would inspect the DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.97,
          "end": 87.81,
          "en": "you would see that the h2 element is actually rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.81,
          "end": 90.363,
          "en": "It just doesn't contain any content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.56,
          "end": 94.59,
          "en": "But rendering an element that has no text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.59,
          "end": 96.15,
          "en": "that's not really great",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.15,
          "end": 99.21000000000001,
          "en": "and typically not something we wanna do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.21000000000001,
          "end": 101.1,
          "en": "It should not be rendered at all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.1,
          "end": 103.143,
          "en": "if we have no selected user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.37,
          "end": 106.5,
          "en": "And that's where another useful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.5,
          "end": 110.13,
          "en": "Angular template feature comes into play.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.13,
          "end": 113.43,
          "en": "Just as we have @for for outputting lists,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.43,
          "end": 116.913,
          "en": "we have @if for outputting conditional content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.35,
          "end": 122.07,
          "en": "Now @if takes a pair of parentheses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.07,
          "end": 124.02,
          "en": "and then between those parentheses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 124.02,
          "end": 127.68,
          "en": "we define the condition we wanna check,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.68,
          "end": 130.29,
          "en": "just as we do it with if statements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.29,
          "end": 132.513,
          "en": "in JavaScript or TypeScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.62,
          "end": 136.573,
          "en": "So here, we could simply check if selectedUser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.003,
          "end": 142.289,
          "en": "is defined or if selectedUserId is defined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 142.289,
          "end": 146.331,
          "en": "but here we can check for the overall selectedUser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.331,
          "end": 148.726,
          "en": "because that will be undefined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 148.726,
          "end": 151.468,
          "en": "if the selectedUserId is undefined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 151.468,
          "end": 152.52100000000002,
          "en": "because in that case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.52100000000002,
          "end": 156.254,
          "en": "find here would yield an undefined value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.254,
          "end": 158.277,
          "en": "So the selectedUser will be undefined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 158.277,
          "end": 160.652,
          "en": "if we don't have an id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 160.652,
          "end": 164.598,
          "en": "And hence here we can check if we do have a selectedUser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 164.598,
          "end": 166.888,
          "en": "so if this is truth.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 166.888,
          "end": 170.03300000000002,
          "en": "And then we add curly braces and then the markup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 170.03300000000002,
          "end": 174.277,
          "en": "that should be rendered if this condition is met.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 174.277,
          "end": 178.121,
          "en": "Now, of course, we know that inside of these curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 178.121,
          "end": 180.42,
          "en": "the selected user will be defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 180.42,
          "end": 184.86,
          "en": "because we only make it in there if we have a selectedUser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 184.86,
          "end": 188.16,
          "en": "Otherwise, this here will not be rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 188.16,
          "end": 190.65,
          "en": "And therefore, we can simplify this code here again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 190.65,
          "end": 192.183,
          "en": "and get rid of this check.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 193.38,
          "end": 195.24,
          "en": "And instead just write it like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 195.24,
          "end": 200.01,
          "en": "and TypeScript with help of Angular does indeed understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 200.01,
          "end": 204.06,
          "en": "that selectedUser will never be undefined in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 204.06,
          "end": 207.15,
          "en": "And hence, we don't have to add any question marks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 207.15,
          "end": 208.82999999999998,
          "en": "or exclamation marks here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 208.82999999999998,
          "end": 210.873,
          "en": "It just works like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 213.09,
          "end": 216.78,
          "en": "Now of course, we might want to show some fallback text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 216.78,
          "end": 219.21,
          "en": "if no user was selected yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 219.21,
          "end": 221.79,
          "en": "and that's why Angular also allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 221.79,
          "end": 225.27,
          "en": "to add a else block with @else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 225.27,
          "end": 228.393,
          "en": "So not just else, but @else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 229.62,
          "end": 232.23,
          "en": "And here, we could then output a paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 232.23,
          "end": 237.23,
          "en": "with an id of fallback maybe for styling purposes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 238.17000000000002,
          "end": 243.17,
          "en": "And then here's say select a user to see their tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 246.21,
          "end": 248.31,
          "en": "With that, if you save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 248.31,
          "end": 252.24,
          "en": "you will see that initially, you'll see that fallback text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 252.24,
          "end": 255.96,
          "en": "but if you now click on a user, you instead see their name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 255.96,
          "end": 258.54,
          "en": "And that, of course, is an improvement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 258.54,
          "end": 262.5,
          "en": "and shows you how you can use if and else",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 262.5,
          "end": 264.573,
          "en": "to render conditional content.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
